# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# TypeScript incremental build caches (tsconfig.tsbuildinfo, plus the
# tsconfig.tests/node variants). Round 17 saw one of these at the repo root and
# could not name the writer: none of the checked-in tsconfigs set `incremental`
# yet. Round 18 (r18-o3) then enabled `incremental` in all three *on purpose* —
# that is what writes them now, as `pnpm gate` / `pnpm build` fingerprints.
# Machine-local, never repository content. Ignored by pattern, so a renamed
# config or a hand-run `tsc --incremental` cannot reintroduce the leak.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Verification screenshots
.shots/

# Local test roots and Python bytecode
.devroot*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Portable packaging output (scripts/pack-portable.ps1)
.pack/
.searchtest/
.launchtest/
.cleartest/

# Screenshot fixture roots. These hold real cloned repositories, so they must
# never be committed: git otherwise picks up each clone as an embedded repo.
.cardshow/
.devshow/
.gittest/

# CDP verification fixture root (scripts/verify-fixes.ps1). Contains fake
# repositories with .git directories, so it must never be committed either.
.cdpfixtures/

# MCP contract-test fixture container (tests/mcp-server.test.ts). Fake repositories
# carrying fake .devhub.json markers, written on every run; a committed copy would make
# git treat them as container content.
.mcpfixtures/

# Settings written by a development run. The portable build keeps this next to
# the executable; in the checkout it lands here, and it is machine state, not
# source.
src-tauri/devhub-config.json
src-tauri/devhub-config.json.bak
src-tauri/devhub-window.json
.tmp-compose-probe/
env.local.ps1

# Same for the operation log and the IDE icon cache: both are derived from this
# machine's installs and history.
src-tauri/devhub-activity.jsonl
src-tauri/cache/

# The repository index the scan maintains per project root. It is derived from a
# directory listing and rebuilt on demand, so it is never source - and a
# development container can legitimately live inside this checkout.
.devhub-index.json

# The watch probe `vite.config.ts` writes to prove its own watcher is alive. It
# removes the file itself; this is only for a dev server killed mid-test.
.devhub-watch-probe.html

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Linked worktrees for parallel development rounds. Both roots the repo actually
# uses: `.worktrees/` and `.wt/`. `.wt/` was previously excluded only via the local
# uncommitted `.git/info/exclude`, so a fresh clone or CI could not reproduce it and
# would pick up a whole second checkout of every stream's files.
.worktrees/
.wt/

# Agent working memory for this project (logs, dated notes). Machine-local
# state, same class as .shots/ and .devroot*/ above — never repository content.
.workbuddy/
.zwork/

# Clone-strategy benchmark scratch root (scripts/clone-bench.ps1). Holds real
# fixture repositories, so it must never be committed.
.clonebench/

# Process-tree probe scratch root (scripts/jobobject-probe.ps1). Holds the PID
# files of the parent/child/grandchild chain it starts, so it must never be
# committed either.
.jobprobe/

# sccache build cache (R1). Lives inside the repo so no build state is written
# to C:. Recreated on first `cargo` run after `env.ps1` sets SCCACHE_DIR.
.sccache-cache/
src-tauri/.sccache-cache/

# Vendored sccache binary. Installed via `cargo install sccache --root
# vendor/sccache` (see the r1 build-cache notes). Machine-local build tooling, not
# source.
vendor/sccache/

# Vendored cargo-outdated binary (r21-R2-1). Installed via `cargo install
# cargo-outdated --locked --root vendor/cargo-outdated` (see the dependency
# ecosystem notes). Machine-local probe tooling, same class as sccache: never
# source, never committed — the exe alone is ~20 MB.
vendor/cargo-outdated/
